I  the Entrepreneurship is one of the  premier creators of jobs small  businesses create jobs  the Entrepreneurship clinic is designed  to represent low and moderate income  entrepreneurs in expanding or even  starting a new business they have the  entrepreneurial spirit they don't always  have the knowledge that it takes to get  through legally and that's what we're  here for but by and large they are here  to take something that they're  passionate about or something very  skilled at and turn it into a viable  living we've worked with such a great  variety of different businesses we've  had hair stylists pet sitters dog  walkers bakers carers people running  internet businesses for the standard  client that wants to come in and start a  business at the very least they're going  to be faced with regulations at the  local and state level the local level  they'll need to get a city business  license here in city of San Diego if  they're operating a home business that's  a separate permit they'll of course have  local taxes to pay they'll have to get a  DBA if they're not operating under their  name there may be other permits that are  required by the city depending on the  type of business it could be inspection  requirements if it has anything to do  with health or food then you're going to  have the county officials coming with  the right to inspect at the state level  of course there are state taxes if there  are any employees you'll have workers  comp to deal with you'll have believer  codes to deal with you'll have  unemployment insurance disability  insurance corporate taxes or entity  taxes I could go on one of the most  heartbreaking stories for me during my  time here his was a we had a client who  had been trained as a cosmetologist and  had worked in salons for a while and  just wasn't really interested in working  for someone else but she couldn't afford  to run her own salon so she came up with  this idea which I thought was brilliant  where she would she would be a mobile  hairdresser she and she primarily wanted  to go to senior homes or senior citizens  there they can't get out they can't get  to their hairdresser and she was going  to do their hair well it turns out that  in the state of California you can only  do hair or pay in a licensed  establishment and these senior homes  were not licensed establishments they  hadn't gone through the hoops necessary  to become licensed establishments and so  this was a business that I think would  have served a lot of consumers a  population that you know there are a lot  of people that still want to get their  hair done well into their 80s and it was  thwarted I mean there was no way that  she was going to be able to do this in a  legal manner and what that meant was not  only that she couldn't do it and this  was a livelihood she couldn't have she  couldn't employ anyone to help her do it  she wouldn't be able to get any  financing if she was able to if she  tried to do it underground it was  basically a you know a business that  never was it's really frustrating to to  work with a client who is really  passionate about their business who  needs to support a family but is faced  with all of these obstacles the business  permits and the licenses and the taxes  and the employment compliance and all of  that it's very frustrating for me to see  and to know what they have ahead of them  because this is something they're  starting the business of something at  the really passionate about one of the  best ways for the state of California to  get back on track financially i think is  to allow businesses to operate and and  operate without all the compliance and  regulatory burdens that they've been  having to suffer under basically the  state needs to lower taxes and decrease  the regulations

